rs","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Doing\n```gdscript\n$Node2D.stash()\n$Node2D.free()\n```\nwill cause a crash of the running instance:\n`godot.macos.editor.dev.arm64(81727,0x2021d2240) malloc: Double free of object 0x120650390`\n`godot.macos.editor.dev.arm64(81727,0x2021d2240) malloc: *** set a breakpoint in malloc_error_break to debug`\nProbably since `$Node2D` will link to the `PlaceholderNode` after the original is stashed.\n```gdscript\nvar node: = $Node2D\n$Node2D.stash()\nnode.free()\n```\nwill work as intended.\n\nI think there should be other null guards in place, too, otherwise the implementation is okay.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121654#pullrequestreview-4760160752","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121654","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121654#pullrequestreview-4760160752"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121654"}},"submitted_at":"2026-07-23T01:52:16Z","commit_id":"b915027f0889175ea8986f2e38a850f9d939641b"}]